      "math_academy_id": "q-182011",
      "sequence_position": 8,
      "problem": "For the sets $X=\\{x,z\\},$ $Y=\\{a,b\\},$ and $Z=X\\times Y,$ determine which of the following statements are true.\n\nI. $(a,x)\\in Z$\n\nII. $(z,a)\\in Z$\n\nIII. $(z,z)\\in Z$",
      "worked_solution": "The Cartesian product $X\\times Y$ consists of all ordered pairs whose first coordinate belongs to $X$ and whose second coordinate belongs to $Y.$\n\nIn this case, the schematic for $X\\times Y$ is shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14123139/assets/b73e7aeb017bd9f7c50f7d110c7933763834eb391ac4a3e97d25f4e587a8a3d4.png)\n\nHence, the set $Z=X\\times Y$ is given by\n\n$$\nZ={(x,a),(x,b),(z,a),(z,b)}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"",
      "answer_fields_complete": true,
